First of all, Happy New Year!

267
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:20,817
It's time for our building's
annual New Year's Mochi Pounding!

268
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:22,080
Yanni Neko! Nyup!

269
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:23,360
I'll pound it!

270
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:27,860
Your job is to pour water on the
mochi and knead it! Got it? Nyup!

271
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:30,657
I understand the landlord
being all excited,

272
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,817
but what's with Yanni being so fired up?

273
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:35,037
Maybe he's paying her in
a bunch of cigarettes.

274
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:38,260
It's way too early in the
morning to be doing this!

275
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:40,460
Let's get it done, Yanni Nicole!

276
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:46,660
Why'd you stop?

277
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:47,757
Is something wrong?

278
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,120
Well, it's just...

279
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,760
Right, let's do this!

280
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,230
Take that!

281
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:55,120
Come on!

282
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:57,040
Here we go!

283
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:58,780
With gusto!

284
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:07,077
They said it was cigarette poisoning.

285
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:09,420
The poor thing was still so young.

286
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:10,997
Here's what I heard.

287
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,139
See that bald guy?

288
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:16,406
Apparently, a cigarette got mixed
into the mochi he was making.

289
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:24,090
Hurry up.

290
00:17:24,180 --> 00:17:26,220
It's time to pound some mochi. Oh.

291
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:29,720
Am I in a time loop?

292
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,300
It's time to pound some mochi.

293
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:48,640
Pound the mochi.

294
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,040
I don't know why it's happening,

295
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:56,020
but I keep repeating the day
of the mochi pounding, and...

296
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,510
Ah!

297
00:17:57,980 --> 00:17:58,810
Amigo!

298
00:17:58,893 --> 00:18:01,160
Someone dies every time.

299
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:05,920
Each day starts off the same way.

300
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,260
Let's bounce the mochi!

301
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:12,005
I don't know how to escape
from this time loop.

302
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:16,200
However, if I can just finish
this mochi pounding peacefully

303
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,959
without anyone dying, then maybe...

304
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:22,320
The weather is awesome for New Year's Day.

305
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,360
Perfect for making mochi.

306
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:26,957
The landlord seems a
little bit sad though.

307
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,637
So, when do we get to dig this stuff?

308
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:29,550
Up until now.

309
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:34,640
Whenever they got close to the
mortar, a fatal accident would happen.

310
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,340
Very well.

311
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:40,756
I just need to do something crazy
enough to keep them all away from it!

312
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:45,220
What the hell are you doing?

313
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:48,307
Just go and fall down,
couple with the mochi.

314
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:51,852
That being stomped around like
a fatal death shot of fire!

315
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:54,304
They should keep everyone away!

316
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:55,510
Huh?

317
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:58,540
No, the cannon sticks are kicking in.

318
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,720
Yanni, don't touch it, it's giant!

319
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,660
Don't come any closer!

320
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:07,240
Yanni, no!

321
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:10,080
He's all strides and no balls! It's done!

322
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,500
Eat it!

323
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:21,817
It was both soft and
hard at the same time.

324
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:22,730
The loop didn't start over.

325
00:19:22,813 --> 00:19:23,643
Has it ended?

326
00:19:23,726 --> 00:19:26,540
Am I the only one that knows
about this loop of fate?

327
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:30,000
You're Otani, right?

328
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,800
We just received a report.

329
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,039
Please come with us to the station.

330
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:48,920
It was the right thing to do.

331
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,281
Chainsmoker cat?

332
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,620
Rise and shine!

333
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:03,155
I thought we'd go get some
Awachi Island burgers today!

334
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,480
It's the new year.

335
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,209
Can't we just relax a bit?

336
00:20:08,060 --> 00:20:09,377
Relaxing was before eight.

337
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:10,397
It's time to get up!

338
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:13,457
And unless you plan on freezing
to death, we need more kerosene.

339
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:14,577
Quit lollygagging!

340
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:15,580
Go and get it!

341
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,540
Gosh, that's such a pain.

342
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,288
Hands off, you dung beetle!

343
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,540
Oh, for crying out loud!

344
00:20:22,780 --> 00:20:23,900
No one's moving!

345
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:25,840
Traffic on a holiday.

346
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:28,737
I swear I'll tear all
these people a new one!

347
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:31,180
See how much Mom loves traffic.

348
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:34,100
She sure is loud with her love. You know,

349
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:37,757
ever since you started living in that
apartment, you've been acting more like her.

350
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,697
Take that back or a whoop your ass!

351
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,074
Shut your damn mouths!

352
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,564
Well, we haven't moved
an inch and I'm starving.

353
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:45,537
We're going home.

354
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,450
Seriously?

355
00:20:46,533 --> 00:20:50,100
Seriously, here's your
homemade Awaji Eileen burger.

356
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:53,557
There's nothing better than being at home.

357
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:56,464
You realize you're the
one who wanted to go out.

358
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:02,476
Kaoruko, did you put on a
few pounds over the holidays?

359
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:05,660
You want my old maternity clothes?

360
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:06,900
I'm not that big.

361
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:09,540
Do you want them, Shumran? Why would I?

362
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:12,797
Oh, you do kind of have
a big butt, though, sis.

363
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,517
If you wear those clothes backwards,

364
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:17,776
The part that's for the belly
will fit over your butt.

365
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,416
Thanks for the food.

366
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,980
There's more burgers if
you want. No, thanks.

367
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:26,396
I'm a cow, remember?

368
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:27,500
I'm done, too.

369
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:32,809
You're not going anywhere!

370
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:34,764
After we eat, it's family time!

371
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:35,880
You crazy?

372
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:39,757
Why don't we all play a board game
together and watch Shinky Geki?

373
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:40,680
Oh, no.

374
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:44,817
We haven't been back home in a good
while, so mom's all needy, isn't she?

375
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:47,060
Okay, I have an idea. You do?

376
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:53,297
I've been working on my beatboxing.

377
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:54,957
I don't give a rat sauce about that.

378
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,637
Now if you lose, that means
you gotta stay longer.

379
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,317
Hooray, let's get this going.

380
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:01,097
I've dumped them shit, darling.

381
00:22:01,180 --> 00:22:04,020
I'm sick of this goddamn house.

382
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,180
Boom, boom, hello, I'm Soonron.

383
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,420
Thank you.

384
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,517
I'm no longer just doing so.

385
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:47,100
Your heart is being. Always.

386
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:49,597
My heart's feeling.

387
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:52,220
My heart is associated with that.

388
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:55,700
What is it?

389
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,077
Why do we use this?

390
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:06,340
They are I'm down on thework I'm
back through I'm down on thework

391
00:23:07,220 --> 00:23:12,161
Or by the way At the corner of the people
I'm down on the road For sure, I just know

392
00:23:21,400 --> 00:24:51,700
Thank you.
